-- title:
--   Adelic box and stabiliser of an order meeting a conjugate
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, and write $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ and $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}=\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}$, where $\mathbb{A}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11), i.e. $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}$, and it is finitely generated; and let $m\in\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}$. For a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $M$, [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox M`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) is the additive subgroup of $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in M$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every height-one prime; [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31)$\,\Lambda\,m$ is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ of elements whose image under $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$ lies in the image of `finiteAdeleBox`$\,\Lambda$ under $x\mapsto mxm^{-1}$; and [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26)$\,M$ is the stabiliser in $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}$ of the underlying set of `finiteAdeleBox`$\,M$. Put $R=\Lambda\sqcap$`conjByFiniteIdele`$\,\Lambda\,m$. The assertion is the conjunction of four statements: (i) `finiteAdeleBox`$\,R$ equals `finiteAdeleBox`$\,\Lambda$ intersected with its image under $x\mapsto mxm^{-1}$; (ii) for every $N\in\mathbb{N}$, if $m\in$`finiteAdeleBox`$\,\Lambda$ and $N\cdot m^{-1}\in$`finiteAdeleBox`$\,\Lambda$ (scalar action of $N$ viewed in $\mathbb{Q}$), then $N\cdot w\in$`finiteAdeleBox`$\,R$ for every $w\in$`finiteAdeleBox`$\,\Lambda$; (iii) `finiteIdeleStabilizer`$\,R\le$`finiteIdeleStabilizer`$\,\Lambda$; and (iv) $m^{-1}um\in$`finiteIdeleStabilizer`$\,\Lambda$ for every $u\in$`finiteIdeleStabilizer`$\,R$.
--
--   This is the adelic description of the intersection of a quaternion order with one of its idelic conjugates: its finite-adelic box is the intersection of the two boxes, it contains $N$ times the box of $\Lambda$ under the usual normalisation of $m$, and its idelic stabiliser lies in that of $\Lambda$ and conjugates into it — the statements underlying the standard local description of Eichler orders. It is used throughout the Čerednik–Drinfel'd coset-graph and tower constructions, for instance when identifying intersections of orders attached to vertices of the graph and recognising them as Eichler orders of the expected level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_finiteAdeleBox_inf_conjByFiniteIdele_eq_and_finiteIdeleStabilizer_le.lean

